  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently validation for archival groups is happening in the AbstractPersister.resolveRootObjectId() class down in the fcrepo-persistence-ocfl module. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It may make more sense for this initial check to happen higher up in the stack, namely that the kernel or HTTP layer.   Be that as it may we still need a way to determine whether a given resource should be nested within an archival group on persist.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "What archival group if any should new fedoraResourceA be nested in? ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The FedoraToOCFLIndex  can tell you for a given fedoraResourceId what  is the fedora identifier associated with the ocfl object root.   We could extend this to maintain a flag indicating whether or not the root identifier is an ArchivalGroup.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Then we could move the AbstractPersister.findArchivalGroupInAncestry() into FedoraToOCFLIndex.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
